WEBVTT

01:27.140 --> 01:29.980
AQUARION

01:32.980 --> 01:34.310
Please say yes!

01:36.390 --> 01:37.620
I'm sorry.

01:39.570 --> 01:39.990
Got it!

01:39.991 --> 01:40.990
Hey, did you hear?

01:40.991 --> 01:43.150
She sank Kuwata-senpai, too!

01:41.240 --> 01:43.410
- I fell in love at first sight when we
passed in the hall - Please go out with me

01:43.150 --> 01:44.260
I'm sorry.

01:44.510 --> 01:45.530
Seriously?

01:45.540 --> 01:46.870
"Will you please go out with me?"

01:45.720 --> 01:48.330
How many has Momohime-sama
turned down anyway?

01:46.960 --> 01:48.210
- Momohime
- "Sorry!"

01:47.310 --> 01:48.329
I'm sorry.

01:48.330 --> 01:51.000
I mean, what kind of guy
does she even go for?

01:49.340 --> 01:50.540
I'm sorry.

01:49.920 --> 01:50.999
Please go out with me

01:51.000 --> 01:52.120
I'm sorry.

01:52.480 --> 01:53.589
I'm sorry!

01:53.590 --> 01:54.950
I'm sorry!

01:56.960 --> 01:58.879
None of the boys around
here are on her level.

01:58.880 --> 02:00.385
Please go out with me!!

02:00.386 --> 02:02.749
I mean, this is Momohime-sama
we're talking about.

02:02.750 --> 02:04.950
I'm sorry!

02:14.450 --> 02:17.910
Oh. So you did know about it.

02:18.130 --> 02:22.399
We actually didn't know
she was going to die.

02:22.400 --> 02:25.909
Huh? But weren't you both at the funeral?

02:25.910 --> 02:30.430
We had no memories of that happening.
We do remember now, though.

02:31.570 --> 02:36.100
Memories are generated by quantum
oscillations in the brain, after all.

02:36.990 --> 02:41.320
They can appear or disappear due
to interference between universes.

02:42.290 --> 02:44.669
Interference between universes?

02:44.670 --> 02:45.670
Yes.

02:45.900 --> 02:49.799
Sometimes people can have different
memories of the same past event.

02:49.800 --> 02:51.940
That is called the Mandela Effect.

02:52.480 --> 02:56.189
But surely this is an interference
fringe of memories

02:56.190 --> 02:58.880
caused by the contact with mythic space.

02:59.610 --> 03:03.990
Satela

02:59.610 --> 03:07.610
Boat Capsizes While Whitebait
Fishing, Captain and Crew Rescued

03:00.250 --> 03:05.559
Yesterday, a boat fishing for whitebait
capsized off the Izu Peninsula.

03:03.991 --> 03:08.370
Off Izu Peninsula

03:05.560 --> 03:07.670
The cause is said to have been high waves.

03:08.720 --> 03:14.039
All of a sudden there was like a big flash
of light... well, at least it felt like it,

03:14.040 --> 03:17.279
and then this huge wave
came crashing down on us.

03:17.280 --> 03:19.960
Beyond that, I have no clue what happened.

03:20.370 --> 03:25.069
Then if we had told you that
we knew she was going to die,

03:25.070 --> 03:27.230
you wouldn't have deployed her?

03:29.090 --> 03:31.500
The causal relationship
works the other way here.

03:32.560 --> 03:38.030
Munakata-sensei deployed Ichiki Sayo-kun
because she did not know she would die.

03:38.370 --> 03:40.120
That's why she died.

03:41.100 --> 03:44.160
The funeral was held in advance.

03:44.730 --> 03:48.330
So that's the universe's
ability to self-correct...

03:53.780 --> 03:55.899
Huh? Momohime-sama?

03:55.900 --> 03:57.500
Why is she on the second-year floor?

04:02.940 --> 04:04.199
Let's go out.

04:04.200 --> 04:04.590
Hm?

04:04.590 --> 04:05.590
Huh?!

04:09.430 --> 04:12.819
What is it?
Why are you dragging me out here?

04:12.820 --> 04:14.429
That hurts!

04:14.430 --> 04:16.770
I remembered about Sayo.

04:17.570 --> 04:18.770
Y-You what?

04:19.280 --> 04:22.060
She was with you, wasn't she?

04:22.790 --> 04:23.230
Where?

04:23.231 --> 04:24.700
Where? Come on...

04:25.750 --> 04:29.079
Saruta-sensei's explanation doesn't
make a lot of sense to me either.

04:29.080 --> 04:30.740
Huh? Really?

04:31.460 --> 04:32.510
Oh.

04:35.620 --> 04:36.620
Hey.

04:37.180 --> 04:39.359
M-Momohime-sama!

04:39.360 --> 04:42.099
Perfect timing.
You guys are both Elements, right?

04:42.100 --> 04:43.790
Y-Yes!

04:44.480 --> 04:48.980
Wait. Haven't I met you guys before?

04:50.330 --> 04:51.330
No.

04:52.610 --> 04:57.530
We have seen you around school,
but we've never talked before.

04:58.300 --> 05:02.810
No, not at school.
Somewhere else, a long time ago.

05:03.270 --> 05:04.450
A long time ago?

05:04.970 --> 05:10.620
It doesn't matter.
Anyway, wasn't Sayo in the Element class?

05:13.190 --> 05:15.799
I knew it! She was!

05:15.800 --> 05:17.450
W-Well, she...

05:23.460 --> 05:25.520
I think this was it.

05:27.530 --> 05:30.630
Oh. Ichiki-san used
to read that book a lot.

05:45.000 --> 05:47.189
Send the maiden to the fountain of soma?

05:47.190 --> 05:48.780
To join the goddesses?

05:49.130 --> 05:53.360
You wish to make a new maiden a goddess?

06:00.750 --> 06:04.379
Could this be? Sedona will be a goddess?

06:04.380 --> 06:05.540
That's absurd!

06:06.130 --> 06:10.210
Rejoice! My daughter shall
join the goddesses!

06:10.610 --> 06:12.010
Dear sister...

06:12.670 --> 06:16.370
My beloved baby sister
Haida, do not be sad.

06:16.730 --> 06:20.490
As a goddess, I will be able to
watch over you for all time.

06:21.390 --> 06:26.180
But does that not mean
that you and he shall...

06:32.100 --> 06:33.459
What?

06:33.460 --> 06:35.330
What just happened?

06:36.350 --> 06:38.560
She had wings.

06:40.010 --> 06:43.339
Isn't DEAVA going to choose
more members to recruit?

06:43.340 --> 06:47.110
I believe she's working
on that in her own way.

06:47.530 --> 06:51.159
Wasn't there another candidate
who was chosen much earlier?

06:51.160 --> 06:52.479
What happened to her?

06:52.480 --> 06:55.229
She is an excellent student.

06:55.230 --> 06:58.809
We all thought she would
be chosen right away.

06:58.810 --> 07:02.789
Yeah, because she has a strong sense of
justice, and her mana balance is perfect.

07:02.790 --> 07:04.739
We couldn't find anything wrong with her.

07:04.740 --> 07:08.170
In fact, that might have
counted against her.

07:09.200 --> 07:13.140
Because lacking emotional balance
is a requirement for Elements?

07:13.760 --> 07:16.529
Regardless, I'd be more worried
if she could be influenced

07:16.530 --> 07:20.360
by psychological attacks from mythic space.

07:20.830 --> 07:24.779
You might be right.
Devils, demons, beasts...

07:24.780 --> 07:28.199
The images of monsters passed down
by different cultures on Earth

07:28.200 --> 07:32.080
are all visions sent from the
Shadow Angels that inhibit mythic space.

07:32.330 --> 07:36.749
Exposure to those psychological
attacks is what has caused humanity

07:36.750 --> 07:38.940
to commit atrocities
and wage terrible wars.

07:39.340 --> 07:42.519
Our goal as the World Awakening Council

07:42.520 --> 07:45.510
is to free the pent-up souls of humanity.

07:47.600 --> 07:50.520
Well, this certainly is troublesome,
Munakata-sensei.

07:50.760 --> 07:52.289
It's amusing, isn't it?

07:52.290 --> 07:55.119
The people who run the world
from behind the scenes

07:55.120 --> 07:58.029
are forced to rely on school children
and this oracle machine

07:58.030 --> 07:59.730
they themselves created.

08:00.540 --> 08:01.790
However...

08:02.860 --> 08:03.850
Hm?

08:03.851 --> 08:06.930
I have a feeling DEAVA is going
to choose the girl after all.

08:08.110 --> 08:09.530
That would be something.

08:10.330 --> 08:12.090
It's just my intuition, though.

08:13.400 --> 08:18.009
So the girl's emotional balance
is missing something?

08:18.010 --> 08:19.550
Is that what you mean?

08:19.900 --> 08:22.870
Perhaps. Who knows?

08:30.600 --> 08:33.220
The Element class is adding a student.

08:33.220 --> 08:35.980
Huh? Who? You mean another elite is born?

08:33.221 --> 08:37.120
Announcement
Amaha Momohime
has been designated
an Element Cadet.

08:36.420 --> 08:37.699
I knew it!

08:37.700 --> 08:38.750
Oh, boy.

08:38.751 --> 08:40.480
I was sure Momo would get picked, too.

08:47.350 --> 08:51.540
Hm. This goes like this, so...

08:52.070 --> 08:54.019
Yeah, I think I'm good.

08:54.020 --> 08:55.020
Here we go!

09:00.510 --> 09:02.610
Huh? Over already?

09:03.090 --> 09:04.230
Good job.

09:04.660 --> 09:05.770
Thank you.

09:07.140 --> 09:10.830
The score doesn't lie. Perfect.

09:11.220 --> 09:14.330
She always was a teacher's pet.

09:14.550 --> 09:19.259
I thought Momohime-senpai would've
been chosen first to be an Element.

09:19.260 --> 09:22.779
How exactly are Elements chosen anyway?

09:22.780 --> 09:24.330
Very good question.

09:24.790 --> 09:27.360
We don't even know ourselves.

09:27.740 --> 09:30.970
But we do have something of a hypothesis.

09:31.930 --> 09:36.440
Students chosen to be Elements all lack
something in regard to emotional balance.

09:36.860 --> 09:41.870
For example, Otori-kun,
in your case, you lack a sense of fear.

09:42.670 --> 09:46.199
And Tsukishiro-kun, for you, it's empathy.

09:46.200 --> 09:47.430
Empathy.

09:48.000 --> 09:51.889
Hatano-kun, you have a very
weak sense of curiosity.

09:51.890 --> 09:53.320
I thought so.

09:53.680 --> 09:56.979
However, when you unite,
you compliment each other

09:56.980 --> 09:59.659
and may be able to turn
it to your advantage.

09:59.660 --> 10:03.820
However, we still don't know
how Amaha-san fits in.

10:04.590 --> 10:09.100
We haven't been able to confirm
that she lacks an emotion.

10:09.620 --> 10:12.169
The hypothesis itself may be flawed

10:12.170 --> 10:16.010
or she may lack something that isn't
so easily measured in battle.

10:23.600 --> 10:24.600
Huh?

10:28.000 --> 10:29.000
What...

10:30.410 --> 10:31.930
was that?

10:38.080 --> 10:40.739
What are we doing here?

10:40.740 --> 10:44.729
Well, Momohime-senpai told
us to meet her here.

10:44.730 --> 10:48.129
Thanks for waiting! I bought lunch for you.

10:48.130 --> 10:50.800
It's from your senpai's
personal favorite, Shonan-do!

10:51.910 --> 10:55.149
The tuna roll has got
to be the most popular.

10:55.150 --> 10:57.670
Shumai and the curry bun
are good too, though.

10:58.300 --> 11:01.039
Uh... Oh. Thanks.

11:01.040 --> 11:03.429
If you want something sweet,

11:03.430 --> 11:05.579
you have your cream bun here
and your sweet bean doughnut.

11:05.580 --> 11:07.489
Oh, can't forget about
the chocolate chip.

11:07.490 --> 11:10.500
Huh? Th-Thank you very much!

11:11.020 --> 11:13.560
And the usual for you, Sakko.

11:14.020 --> 11:16.439
Here. Meat cutlet and a yakisoba bun.

11:16.440 --> 11:17.600
Thank you.

11:18.310 --> 11:21.510
Anyway, it's my treat. Eat up, eat up!

11:29.170 --> 11:32.430
Now Rimiya-kun, Toshi-kun, Sakko...

11:38.260 --> 11:39.850
Let's settle this once and for all.

11:45.800 --> 11:48.360
Munakata-sensei told me everything.

11:48.790 --> 11:51.650
You guys were defending
the planet, weren't you?

11:53.060 --> 11:59.160
But Sayo didn't die in an accident.
She died in battle alongside you.

11:59.510 --> 12:02.660
I realize that it wasn't your fault.

12:03.280 --> 12:06.909
Nor was it Munakata-sensei's
fault for deploying her.

12:06.910 --> 12:10.070
I get it. I get it, but still...

12:10.470 --> 12:12.470
I can't just let it go.

12:14.690 --> 12:15.920
Momohime...

12:16.780 --> 12:19.150
But I feel a lot better today.

12:19.510 --> 12:24.540
If I'd never found out, this feeling
would have haunted me forever.

12:25.550 --> 12:33.390
But it was still a little frustrating to
realize my memories had been edited.

12:34.440 --> 12:38.170
I always thought of
Sayo as a little sister.

12:38.630 --> 12:43.640
So I can't believe I couldn't
even remember how she died.

12:45.280 --> 12:46.670
Senpai...

12:47.100 --> 12:51.679
Um, apparently, I actually lack empathy,

12:51.680 --> 12:55.710
so I can't really relate to your feelings
or Ichiki-san's feelings very well.

12:56.500 --> 12:57.600
Rimiya-kun...

12:58.880 --> 13:02.429
But I do have a feeling Ichiki-san
was happy at the end.

13:02.430 --> 13:05.780
Uh, but she said she didn't want to die.

13:06.660 --> 13:10.180
I don't... want to die.

13:11.260 --> 13:12.420
Yeah, that's why.

13:13.220 --> 13:16.490
The thing she lacked was self-love.

13:18.240 --> 13:22.229
Oh, right. She said she didn't want to die

13:22.230 --> 13:25.109
because she finally understood
what it meant to value herself.

13:25.110 --> 13:26.139
Yeah.

13:26.140 --> 13:30.889
They say the Vector Machines are made from
Mythic Star Stones that can transmit mana.

13:30.890 --> 13:33.729
Maybe Ichiki-san was able to
regain an emotion she lacked

13:33.730 --> 13:36.079
because our mana was flowing through them.

13:36.080 --> 13:40.640
Then if we keep fighting together,
maybe someday...

13:47.360 --> 13:49.470
Okay, that settles it!

13:51.080 --> 13:51.980
Huh?

13:51.980 --> 13:52.470
Hmm?

13:52.471 --> 13:55.759
I'm going to help defend
the planet with you!

13:55.760 --> 13:57.489
Momohime-senpai...

13:57.490 --> 14:01.029
I'll do everything I can.

14:01.030 --> 14:04.550
I won't let any of you die.
You'd better not die on me, okay?

14:05.200 --> 14:08.790
Not you, Sakko, or you,
Toshi-kun, or you, Rimiya-kun.

14:09.140 --> 14:10.230
And that's a promise!

14:10.620 --> 14:13.400
O-Okay!

14:15.680 --> 14:17.750
Hey, wait!

14:18.060 --> 14:20.959
Bring back my Shonan dog!

14:20.960 --> 14:23.940
Whoa, wait! Come back right now!

14:23.941 --> 14:25.410
See? Isn't that just perfect?

14:25.840 --> 14:30.740
It's hard to believe that
she lacks an emotion, too.

14:35.600 --> 14:41.059
And Chako here was so sleepy,
when she answered she said, "Yes, Mom."

14:41.060 --> 14:42.190
Hey, cut it out!

14:45.220 --> 14:46.689
Rimiya-kun?

14:46.690 --> 14:51.070
Uh, it's nothing.
I'm gonna head back to class.

14:51.450 --> 14:52.720
Oh, okay.

15:00.870 --> 15:02.280
- Whoa!
- Oh!

15:02.283 --> 15:03.659
Rimiya-kun!

15:03.660 --> 15:04.910
Senpai.

15:05.290 --> 15:06.899
Let's work hard tomorrow, okay?

15:06.900 --> 15:07.800
G'night!

15:07.801 --> 15:10.210
Yeah, good... night.

15:26.600 --> 15:31.369
Ru and his younger sister Hina were
living on the isle of Tahiti.

15:31.370 --> 15:33.860
When they ran out of food on the island,

15:34.140 --> 15:39.070
Ru built a boat, and they took to
the sea in search of a new island.

15:39.730 --> 15:44.379
One night, Hina looked up at the
beautiful full moon in the sky,

15:44.380 --> 15:48.970
and then without thinking,
hoisted sail and set sail alone.

15:50.010 --> 15:55.950
The boat rose higher and higher in the
sky until it finally reached the moon.

15:56.600 --> 16:01.310
Ru lamented the loss of his sister,
but Hina never returned.

16:02.170 --> 16:06.069
Hina became the goddess of the moon
and remains there even today,

16:06.070 --> 16:10.730
where she continues to craft clothes with
tapa cloth made from the bark of trees.

16:12.730 --> 16:15.950
The boat is probably her wings.

16:16.180 --> 16:17.340
Wings?

16:17.650 --> 16:19.819
Like the celestial maiden's
robe of feathers,

16:19.820 --> 16:25.170
there are all sorts of myths around the
Pacific Ocean about people with wings.

16:27.930 --> 16:33.130
I bet in our previous lives, we all
had wings, too. I'm sure of it.

16:39.630 --> 16:42.730
Hey, Sakko. I told you this was dangerous.

16:45.400 --> 16:46.870
Is something wrong?

16:47.250 --> 16:48.550
It's nothing.

16:48.930 --> 16:49.930
Huh?

16:53.270 --> 16:57.810
I keep warning you about parkour, but you
don't have any intention of quitting, do you?

16:58.160 --> 16:59.910
Is it because you lack fear?

17:00.530 --> 17:02.509
Well, you're not gonna change now.

17:02.510 --> 17:05.149
You've been like this since primary school.

17:05.150 --> 17:09.490
Sayo and I have told you to stop
so many times, but you never listen.

17:13.550 --> 17:18.650
Hey, Sakko. You'd better
not leave me too, okay?

17:20.230 --> 17:23.630
Don't go dying on me when
I'm not paying attention.

17:28.070 --> 17:29.320
Anyway, here you go.

17:29.860 --> 17:30.860
Huh?

17:31.270 --> 17:33.349
It's a good luck charm
from the Enoshima Shrine.

17:33.350 --> 17:34.520
I got it for you.

17:35.760 --> 17:39.689
That other day, you just rushed
in head first without thinking

17:39.690 --> 17:41.640
and then Toshi-kun got injured, right?

17:42.210 --> 17:44.790
I can't help it. I'm just not afraid.

17:45.550 --> 17:48.369
Nobody is saying that's your fault.

17:48.370 --> 17:51.659
But it's dangerous if you keep this up.
I just want you to be careful.

17:51.660 --> 17:52.700
Ugh.

17:53.470 --> 17:56.519
Which one of us hasn't changed
at all since primary, again?

17:56.520 --> 17:57.520
Huh?

17:57.590 --> 18:02.499
Whenever I saw you, you would say, "it's
dangerous," "cut it out," or, "take it easy."

18:02.500 --> 18:04.410
You were always such a downer.

18:05.530 --> 18:09.799
And you're still acting like you think
you're my big sister, Momo-nee.

18:09.800 --> 18:12.809
Huh? You're sure one to talk.

18:12.810 --> 18:14.330
Right back at you.

18:22.500 --> 18:25.950
It would be best for Hatano-kun to go,
since he has live combat experience.

18:26.200 --> 18:29.330
But his arm is still injured.

18:31.110 --> 18:32.539
Then I'll go!

18:32.540 --> 18:33.540
Huh?

18:35.230 --> 18:39.279
Iwaya cave, launch sequence
initiated. Bay doors opened.

18:39.280 --> 18:41.579
Vector magnetically coupled with shuttle.

18:41.580 --> 18:43.800
Vector Tir, launching!

18:48.400 --> 18:51.320
Bridge catapult, activate launch sequence.

18:51.620 --> 18:53.820
Release bridge and raise lifts.

18:54.210 --> 18:56.510
Vector magnetically coupled with shuttle.

18:57.040 --> 18:59.250
Vector Siegel, launching!

19:03.830 --> 19:06.500
Yacht harbor, launch sequence initiated.

19:06.840 --> 19:08.329
Prepare for launch.

19:08.330 --> 19:10.910
Electromagnetic catapult cover opened.

19:11.360 --> 19:12.740
Rails extended.

19:13.340 --> 19:15.490
Vector Feoh, launching!

19:22.920 --> 19:25.930
So that's a real Mythic Beast.

19:26.650 --> 19:28.179
I'll distract it again.

19:28.180 --> 19:30.499
Hold on, Sakko! Wait up!

19:30.500 --> 19:33.309
I can be the decoy. You should pull back!

19:33.310 --> 19:34.859
But I'm already too far in!

19:34.860 --> 19:37.879
Momohime-senpai, Sakko is correct.

19:37.880 --> 19:40.280
All right, then. Thanks, Rimiya-kun.

19:40.970 --> 19:42.080
Uh, sure!

19:43.220 --> 19:48.200
Due to his lack of empathy, Tsukishiro-kun
is able to make decisions unemotionally.

19:49.080 --> 19:52.910
And Amaha-san was able to regain
her cool after taking his advice.

19:53.320 --> 19:55.990
Target's high-dimensional quantum
response is increasing.

19:56.190 --> 19:59.010
Target's high-dimensional quantum
response is increasing.

20:04.100 --> 20:05.210
Sakko!

20:08.300 --> 20:09.490
Damn it!

20:13.010 --> 20:15.679
Let's unite! Sakko, Rimiya-kun!

20:15.680 --> 20:16.670
- Yes!
- Yeah!

20:19.280 --> 20:20.890
Let's do it, guys!

20:21.380 --> 20:24.700
Mythic Star Union! Go, Aquarion!

20:37.080 --> 20:41.680
This must be their...
I've never felt anything like this!

20:49.400 --> 20:50.720
Oh!

20:51.430 --> 20:53.630
Momohime-senpai!

20:57.570 --> 20:59.420
Aquarion Feoh!

21:02.390 --> 21:03.719
It's coming, Momo-nee!

21:03.720 --> 21:04.720
Yeah!

21:05.250 --> 21:06.250
You got it!

21:07.850 --> 21:09.370
Senpai, be careful!

21:11.730 --> 21:13.130
Thanks, Rimiya-kun!

21:23.610 --> 21:25.300
Good! They've got it now!

21:26.740 --> 21:30.179
I can feel their thoughts inside me.

21:30.180 --> 21:32.310
But what are these...

21:32.910 --> 21:35.200
feelings I don't understand?

21:35.840 --> 21:39.309
They feel kind of... gross!

21:39.310 --> 21:40.430
Huh?

21:42.580 --> 21:44.790
What's happening to them?

21:49.610 --> 21:50.610
What?

21:50.870 --> 21:53.290
Target's high-dimensional quantum
response is increasing.

21:54.270 --> 21:56.789
Listen, Sakko! Wait for an opening!

21:56.790 --> 21:57.210
Yeah.

